WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.600
Jirukoma left Komain as chief
of the settlement,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.930
and together with the others
who volunteered to go,

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.020
put Friedonia behind him.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.360
Those who departed could not shake
their longing for home,

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.030
and would try to take back their lands,
by force, if necessary,

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.650
while those who saw them off kept
their longing for home in their hearts,

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.580
and dreamed of restoring the peace
of their nations in a foreign land.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:47.330
Their parting was a sad one,
but it was their choice.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.550
<i>"...Keep on going anyway"</i>

00:00:51.550 --> 00:01:00.600
<i>Our bond strikes deep into my left breast</i>

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.440
<i>We enjoy a fleeting happiness</i>
<i>after weathering one fog,</i>

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.440
<i>until our vision becomes obscured again</i>

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.410
<i>Bitterly betrayed, we grow</i>
<i>disgusted by our destiny</i>

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:25.290
<i>But why does the dawn still come?</i>

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:30.630
<i>We close our eyes and try to remember</i>

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:35.970
<i>the chance of stopping, of never meeting</i>

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:41.550
<i>From boundless zero to infinity,</i>

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:47.060
<i>dreaming is the heartbeat of believing</i>

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.900
<i>We'll move along alone and in pairs</i>

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:57.030
<i>Don't stay put; our small,</i>
<i>though by no means helpless steps</i>

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.830
<i>will open uncharted territory</i>
<i>for each of us</i>

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:07.910
<i>Realize we will never again</i>
<i>let our dreams die on the vine</i>

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:14.710
<i>The tear tracks that run down</i>
<i>our cheeks are shooting stars</i>

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:18.550
<i>We're going to grab hold of them</i>

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.350
"Know Your Enemy and Know Yourself,
and Your Union Shall Not Be Endangered"

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:26.390
I see that everyone is here.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.940
Oh, these glasses?

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.360
These are not prescription lenses.
They just put me in the right mood.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.270
Is it a matter of mood?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:38.530
Yes. For you see, the reason
I had you all come here today

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.950
is for you to attend Lesson 1 of
your "Fiancée's Bridal Course."

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:49.660
And your teacher will, of course,
be myself, Excel Walter.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.960
I have been hoping for an opportunity
such as this for a long time,

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:59.670
and when I heard His Majesty say that
he could have children any time now,

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.010
I decided that now would be
the perfect time.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.970
After all, in time,
all of you will be mothers.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.600
As you are aware, following the death
of the king two generations ago,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.270
the Kingdom of Elfrieden
nearly faced a civil war

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:17.900
surrounding the royal family's dispute
over succession to the throne.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.530
I trust that such a thing will not happen
under the reign of His Majesty Souma.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.280
However, we must not be complacent!

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.240
If there is any breach between
king and queen,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.700
or between any of the queens,

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.120
there will certainly be someone who
will try to take advantage of it!

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.460
For the sake of the kingdom,

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:40.300
it is necessary for you to establish
harmonious marital relationships.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:45.680
That is what this bridal
training course is for.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.930
Excuse me, but why are you
teaching us, Duchess Walter?

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.730
Well, I <i>have </i>lived for over
500 years, now.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.820
I have fallen in love with
a number of gentlemen,

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:01.990
and I have never parted with any of them,
except through death.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.820
I have also born each of them children.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:11.120
I will now teach each of you as
queens--no, as individual women

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.790
the way to remain with
the man that you love.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.300
How to be a wife, from understanding
the psychology of the male mind,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:24.760
to ensuring a smooth married life via
the performance of nighttime "services."

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:31.020
I have already had His Majesty Souma
take an individual class with me.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:38.730
Now, in both war and marriage,
information is essential.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:42.490
"Know your enemy and know yourself,
and in a hundred battles,

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.360
you shall not be endangered," is something
His Majesty is fond of saying.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.160
That's right. If you know how
the other party views you,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.000
it will become clear to you
how to conduct yourself.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.420
There are times when it is
good to be unpredictable,

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.210
and create some space between you
to shake things up if you're in a rut.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:04.090
Know your enemy and know yourself,
and your union shall not be endangered.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.050
After my lesson with His Majesty,

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:14.640
I called in an illusionist mage to
secretly cast a confession spell on him.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:19.270
This notebook contains the information
I got out of His Majesty at the time.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:30.990
All right, allow me to tell each of you
how His Majesty Souma sees you.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.950
Roroa...

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:37.040
I'll start with his estimation of you.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.170
Wh-Why me?!

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.250
No special reason.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.050
I just thought I'd start with
the latest one to meet His Majesty.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:49.640
Well, I <i>am </i>the newest one of this group...

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.220
I suppose it's better than
having to go last.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.890
All right, according to His Majesty...

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.650
What do you think about Roroa?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:05.360
I like how cheerful and friendly Roroa is.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.490
She can be a bit underhanded,
but that's just part of her charm.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.830
The way she looks up to Liscia and
the others as sisters is heartwarming.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:17.750
Also, she's a wiz when it
comes to finances.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.080
I really am glad that she
became one of my fiancées.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:27.670
Th-This is so embarrassing...

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:33.390
Further, when I asked His Majesty,
"Do you have any feelings for Roroa?"

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:38.310
he answered, "I feel bad that I'm
responsible for her father's death."

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.810
I realize it was war,
but that notwithstanding,

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:46.030
from where she stands, his blood
will always be on my hands.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:49.950
Roroa says that she was
far removed from her father,

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.740
but what if, really,
she doesn't want to marry me?

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.410
That's something he worries
about at times.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.460
Wh-What is he, dense?!

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:04.460
Darling, you dummy!
I've already considered all that!

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:10.130
I want to be with Darling of my own
free will, so why would he say that?!

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:16.970
Roroa...

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.680
Cia...

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:24.770
I get it. I'll have to give Souma
a piece of my mind later.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:28.110
Roroa, the reason His Majesty
thinks the way he does

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:31.570
is because he loves and treasures you.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.740
You do know that, don't you?

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.910
Mm-hmm.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:40.000
So while on the one hand, I'm upset
that he doesn't know how I feel,

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:45.750
I'm also kind of happy to know
that Darling thinks so much of me.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.840
If you know that much,
you should do just fine.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.170
Next up, Juna...

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.340
Yes?

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:59.640
Pretty... Beautiful...
That's the long and short of it.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.600
I don't just mean her appearance,
either; I mean her heart, too.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:09.400
It seems like she keeps a pace behind
the others, to see the larger picture.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:14.860
She truly is the perfect woman.
I don't want to lose her to anyone.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.370
His Majesty said that about me?

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:23.210
When I asked him:
"How do you feel about Juna?"

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:24.920
he said "I sure feel lucky
to be a younger guy

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:29.130
when she lets me dote on her
from time to time."

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:32.760
But I thought His Majesty
and myself were the same age.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.180
She's right. They're both 19.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.560
His Majesty realized something later on.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:46.150
It seems that in his world,
one year lasts for 365 days.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:50.900
Here, it lasts for 384 days,
so as a result of that difference,

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.360
in the world where His Majesty
Souma is from,

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.240
you would be at least a year
older than him.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.450
You mean, I'm a whole year older?

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:03.500
You're not saying that His Majesty
dislikes older women, are you?!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:08.750
Not to worry. His Majesty Souma
also said the following:

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.050
"Where I'm from, we have a saying--

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.170
'Find a wife a year older than you,

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:17.800
even if you must wear
wire sandals to do so'."

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.430
Thank goodness.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.180
Next up, Aisha...

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.730
Y-Yes?

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:27.850
His Majesty Souma's
appraisal of you, Aisha, is...

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:33.320
U-Um, why did you stop there?

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.650
Well, it's...

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.780
..."pet-like."

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.030
It's what?!

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.080
I can see that.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:47.080
Juna, not you, too!
What am I, his pet dog?!

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:51.460
Aisha is a strong, noble,
and beautiful warrior.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:55.670
It's safe to say that she is the most
valiant fighter in the kingdom.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:59.680
It is reassuring to have
Aisha by my side...

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.220
At least it should be...

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:06.020
There's something irresistible about her.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:09.480
I find myself wanting to
protect <i>her</i>, I suppose.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.780
Wah! I'm a failure as a bodyguard!

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:15.940
Ai, shake.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:17.820
Woof.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.700
Aisha, you're adorable.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:22.450
I feel like I want to protect you, myself.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:25.080
Huh? Is that so?

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.000
Ahem...

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:31.040
Lastly, we come to Princess Liscia.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:36.800
I should probably start with what he said
when I asked how he felt about you.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.340
Huh? Why am I the only one you're
answering that question first with?

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.810
I believe his assessment of you,
Princess Liscia,

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.480
can be summarized by
the answer to that one question.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.150
His Majesty answered with one word:

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.110
"Nothing."

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.900
"Nothing"? At all?

00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:00.660
He had something to say about
all the others, didn't he?

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.410
And yet he said "nothing"
when it came to me?

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:07.540
His Majesty said the following:

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:12.170
"I want to <i>personally </i>tell her
the feelings that matter most to me."

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:19.590
You know, it doesn't seem fair that Cia
is the only one he said that about.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.550
Huh?

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.720
I'm jealous that you're the one
who gets special treatment.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:27.140
Ow...! Hey, ladies, that smarts!

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:30.140
Oh, Juna, not you, too!

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:33.360
Roroa, I'm actually a little jealous
of the rest of you, too.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.270
Huh? You are?

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.650
I wanted to hear him say that he
liked such-and-such about me,

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:43.280
or that he didn't want to lose me to
anyone, or he wanted to protect me, too.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.950
I guess that's just the way
these things go.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:50.660
In any case, let's all gather around
the table together from now on!

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:53.380
Ai, way to bring it all together.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.500
Sure!

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:00.970
All right, I would now like to instruct
you on some specific details

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.760
to help you all maintain
your marital bliss.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.810
Specific details?

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.970
I said at the beginning

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.430
that this course would cover
the psychological aspects,

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.440
as well as the performance of
one's nighttime services, did I not?

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.900
And I intend to teach you
<i>exhaustively </i>about those.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:22.030
E-Excuse me, Grandmother,
but everything else aside,

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:25.570
are you sure we have
to sit through a lecture

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.240
on these, um, n-nighttime services?

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.660
I-I'm with Juna on this.
It's just so embarrassing.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.960
I'm kind of curious.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:35.920
Roroa?

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.630
Huh? Cia, you don't wanna know more?

00:12:38.630 --> 00:12:40.550
Well, I mean...

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:45.010
You <i>are </i>a little curious,
aren't you? Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:49.180
Goodness, are you sure you want to
pass up an opportunity such as this?

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:52.350
If you will sit through my lecture
all the way to the end,

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:56.190
then as proof of completion,
I will give you this.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.900
"Top secret document"?

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:02.360
"Burn after reading"?

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.950
Sounds pretty dangerous.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.610
What are they, state secrets?

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:09.280
Yes, top national security secrets.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:14.870
Contained in here are the unspeakable
things that His Majesty Souma

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:18.750
wants you to do to him,
or that he wants to do to you,

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:21.550
as well as the situations
in which to do them.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:24.050
You see? Top national security secrets.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.630
--Oh...
--Oh...

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:28.260
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.640
His Majesty Souma's desires
for each of you,

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:34.020
which he normally keeps under restraint
and locked inside his heart,

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:37.270
are all frankly spelled out
and laid bare in here.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:41.230
Very well, let's begin
the "servicing" lecture.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:03.130
"Gran Chaos Empire,
Imperial Capital, Valois"

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.720
Come in.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.260
Pardon the intrusion.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:20.770
I have a report for you concerning
the slave traders.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.580
So, what about the slave traders?

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.830
Right. As Souma proposed,

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:40.040
I would like to start an approval system
for slave traders here in the empire, too.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.710
That's Souma for you.
Rather than abolishing it outright,

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.760
he made slave traders public servants,

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:49.340
as well as raised the level
of education for slaves.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:51.640
That couldn't have been easy to think up.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:56.270
It wasn't His Majesty; I heard it was
the idea of a slave trader in town.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:15:00.600
Oh, my. I see they are as blessed
with talented people as ever.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.360
That they are.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:06.610
However, there's also a chance that
slave traders who become unsanctioned

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:10.160
may commit violent acts
and start kidnapping people.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.700
It actually happened in Friedonia.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.990
We will have to keep
a careful watch out for that.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:20.330
Right. I would like to bear that
in mind while doing certifications.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:25.750
I have to wonder, what kind of nation
building will Souma try next?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:30.430
He's probably imagining an even
more wonderful kingdom.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:33.970
Sister, you certainly are
taken with Souma.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.390
Of course I am. However,

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:39.730
Fredonia's nation building is
ultimately just for reference.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:44.520
We must build our own rock-solid nation.

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:53.820
Understood. I would like to keep in
close touch with Hakuya going forward.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:58.790
Yes, please do. So, how is it going?

00:15:58.790 --> 00:15:59.790
Huh?

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.620
With Hakuya, I mean.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.210
Th-Th-There's nothing going on!

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.590
Please excuse me.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.920
That's okay. Please continue.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:13.260
The citizens' lives have
become more stable,

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:16.550
allowing us to build many more houses.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:17.810
That's great.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:19.770
But there is a problem.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.270
The trees surrounding the capital
have all been cut down,

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:26.820
both for lumber and
winter heating purposes.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:29.570
Some areas have been left as bare hills.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:33.820
I didn't see that coming. I guess
we introduce lumber stoppages.

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.490
Lumber stoppages?

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:40.410
Where I'm from, lumber was once
an important military resource,

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:44.330
so there were some mountains set
aside where logging was prohibited.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:48.040
It was so strict, they say that felling
a single tree could cost you your head.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.010
<i>That </i>seems a bit excessive...

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.220
We won't go <i>that </i>far.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.720
Beyond that, let's redirect
the thinned timber

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:57.510
from the God-Protected Forest
to where it's needed.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:59.100
Very well.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.560
How are Komain and
the other refugees doing?

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.190
Their relocation to Venetinova
is going smoothly.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:12.240
They seem to have no complaints
with the housing. The issue is jobs.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:16.110
There are many hunters among them,
so the truth is,

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:19.910
there are not many of them with what
you would call "marketable skills."

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:24.330
We can't exactly have them making nothing
but bows, arrows, and spears.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:27.580
They may be hunters, but they
also make woolen goods, right?

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:30.630
Let's put them to work
in the textile industry.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:36.260
We have to invest in the public sector
more, and not just to employ <i>them</i>.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:41.510
Luckily, there are some areas in
Venetinova that have not been zoned.

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:45.100
We can develop the facilities we need
to provide employment for the refugees.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:51.190
Go right ahead. In time, Venetinova
will become a center of trade.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.440
Unless we raise the level
of education there,

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.410
they won't be able to make ends
meet on industry alone.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.990
I've already spoken
with Ginger about that.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:04.370
Leave it to you, Hakuya.
No flies on you, huh?

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:11.380
Y-Your Majesty!

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.750
What's the matter, Poncho?

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:17.430
I-It's finally ready--the thing
Your Majesty requested!

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.260
What?! You don't mean... <i>it</i>?!

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:20.760
Yes!

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:23.930
This is it?

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.980
Please have a taste, yes!

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.320
What do you think?

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:47.250
You did it, Poncho! This is a sauce for
flour-based dishes! No doubt about it!

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.290
Yes!

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:53.460
Begging your pardon, but what
is sauce for flour-based dishes?

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:56.420
Now that we have this, we can make
<i>yakisoba</i>, <i>okonomiyaki</i>, <i>monjayaki</i>,

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:59.300
<i>takoyaki</i>, <i>sobameshi</i>--all of it!

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:02.470
It'll even be good as a sauce
poured over fried foods!

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:04.180
Hakuya, would you like a taste?

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:24.700
It has a fruity, veggie flavor, the aroma
of spices that entices the nose,

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:27.540
and yet it's unlike
ordinary Worcester sauce,

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:31.620
in that it has a strong sweet
and sour flavor and depth of taste.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:34.840
It is indeed unlike any sauce
I've tasted before.

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:37.670
I have to admit,
I'm surprised you reproduced it.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:40.010
You've never even tried it
yourself, either.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:43.390
Thank you very much, yes!

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:46.260
Still, what's in this, anyway?

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.480
I remember tasting it somewhere before.

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:52.810
I'm impressed, Your Majesty.
You took note of it, I see.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.360
I took a mixture of Worcester
and tomato sauce

00:19:55.360 --> 00:20:01.610
and added a little bit of soy sauce
and mirin from Kikkoro Distillery, yes.

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:07.080
Poncho, are you able to
mass-produce this sauce?

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:10.750
Kikkoro Distillery says
they're willing to take it on.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.000
Your Majesty, I just had a thought.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.880
What if we took food that uses
this flour-based-dish sauce

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.760
and made it the specialty dish
of Venetinova?

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:23.430
The creation of new jobs!

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:27.060
We can't let Venetinova have
a monopoly on this sauce,

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:30.020
but it <i>is </i>a gulf city!
They can make squid <i>yakisoba</i>!

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:33.690
This is the dawn of the Venetinova
delicacy, squid <i>yakisoba</i>!

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.690
Squid <i>yakisoba</i>? That sounds so tempting!

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:41.360
I'm sure it will taste good
before I even eat any, yes!

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:48.540
This sure has been a turbulent year, huh?

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.000
Sure has.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.210
I had the throne relinquished
to me on April 32nd,

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:56.000
and before you know it,
another year has passed.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:03.050
Tomorrow is December 32nd. The last
eight months really have flown by.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:12.770
Liscia, is something wrong?

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:15.770
I-It's nothing! It's nothing.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:17.190
Hmm...

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:19.480
Here. "Ahh."

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:26.240
I've always wanted to do this.

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:31.200
You know, sit under the <i>kotatsu</i>,
stay warm and do nothing.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.120
It's terrific, isn't it?

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:35.830
Mm-hmm.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.920
Here. "Ahh."

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:44.800
It's nice to just do nothing.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.930
I hope it stays just
being nothing, though.

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:50.850
Yeah...

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:58.060
And as soon as we say
it's nice to do nothing...

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.520
Yes?

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:06.150
I have a message from Albert.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:09.370
Tomorrow, the evening of December 32nd,

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:12.080
he would like to meet with Your Majesty.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:13.410
At last...

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.460
Father?

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:17.620
Souma, I'm coming with you.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:20.630
He requests that His Majesty comes alone.

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:39.060
<i>"What are we supposed to choose?"</i>

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:44.320
<i>Our voices imploring the future are hoarse</i>

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>We've become so afraid</i>
<i>of what we could lose</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.370
<i>that we're just frozen in place</i>

00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:59.830
<i>How many times have we made mistakes</i>

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:05.800
<i>because we wanted to check our "answers"?</i>

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:13.140
<i>Before we knew it we were in love,</i>
<i>we had fallen in love</i>

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:17.390
<i>I'll hold fast to you</i>
<i>in the times we're in</i>

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:23.190
<i>We who set alight</i>
<i>our finite lives to fight</i>

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:28.450
<i>are noble and beautiful above all</i>

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:32.410
<i>As long as we create</i>
<i>as many bright tomorrows</i>

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:37.750
<i>as the indelible wounds we suffer,</i>

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:46.800
<i>we can be proud of all</i>
<i>we've woven together</i>
